From: pocket-debs <masterxq@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] plasma-dialer: choose the SIM of a call
Description:
 With more than one modem the dialer chose no modem ("TODO: select device
 uni"): dialling, USSD and the controls of the call screen did nothing.
 .
 SimUtils lists the active SIM of every modem with its slot (PrimarySimSlot,
 read over D-Bus), name ("SIM <slot>", else the operator name) and icon
 (shared with plasma-nm and spacebar in simidentitiesrc, class
 SimIdentities). The default SIM for calls is a setting (by ICCID), the
 first SIM without a choice. With several SIMs the call button calls
 through the default SIM and carries the icon of that SIM as a badge; the
 so far empty cell left of it holds a smaller, tinted call button for the
 other SIM, or with three and more SIMs one that opens a choice. One tap is
 one call, nothing is remembered. USSD goes through the default SIM. The
 call history offers a call back button through the SIM of the call (the
 SIM identifier stored with each call). With one SIM nothing changes.
Forwarded: no
License: as the patched files (LGPL-2.0-or-later, GPL-2.0-or-later, LicenseRef-KDE-Accepted-GPL); new files simutils.*, CallButton.qml LGPL-2.0-or-later, simidentities.* LGPL-2.1-only OR LGPL-3.0-only OR LicenseRef-KDE-Accepted-LGPL
Last-Update: 2026-11-25
